infographic sequence-snake-steps-underline-text
data
  title Storage tiering: signals age into cheaper tiers
  desc Cost per byte falls ~10x per tier, so retention cost grows logarithmically, not linearly
  sequences
    - label Tier 0 · 24–48h buffer
      desc Kafka / Pulsar / NATS · raw full resolution · ~1000x cost per byte
    - label Tier 1 · 7–14 day hot query
      desc Tempo / Loki / Prometheus / Pyroscope · incident window · ~100x cost per byte
    - label Tier 2 · 30–90 day rollup
      desc 5-min recording rules · traces 1% + 100% errors · ~10x cost per byte
    - label Tier 3 · 90 days–7 yr archive
      desc Object storage S3 / GCS · full fidelity for compliance · ~1x baseline cost
theme
  palette #f43f5e #f59e0b #0ea5e9 #10b981
